{"id": "q0032", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1851623335, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "It takes John 5 minutes to get to the first side of the Rubik's cube.  The second and third sides each take twice that long.  The last 2 sides each take half as long as the first, and once you get the 5th side you have all 6 sides.  How long does the Rubik's cube take?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0032.wav", "input_sha256": "dd6bb8eaf3ba4d96a20484261431d205031c7d63946e979d8a2fd7d9fc942c2e", "input_samples": 330400, "input_s": 20.65, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.2587, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So the first side takes 5 minutes. The second and third sides each take twice that long, so 10 minutes each. That' s 2 0 minutes for both of them combined. The last two sides each take half as long as the first, which is 2. 5 minutes each, so that's 5 minutes total for those two. Add ing it all up: 5 plus 20 plus 5 equals 3 0 minutes. So the Rubik's cube takes 30 minutes.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 25, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0032_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "99d697959aa0334d710edda90dce2cea5cf234bbad45cc66dd2f547c87681a30", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.28}}, "chunks