{"id": "q0115", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3284998833, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "In the land of Ink, the money system is unique. One Trinket is equal to 4 Blinkets, and 3 Blinkets are equal to 7 Drinkets. In Trinkets, what is the value of 56 Drinkets?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0115.wav", "input_sha256": "425f92be59171877dec281c6414f9619dfde45f63ec7c9755b417a80bd6f497e", "input_samples": 209600, "input_s": 13.1, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.4445, "act": 0.9982, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we' re told that one trinket is equal to four blanket s. And three blankets are equal to seven drinkets. So let's figure out how many drink ets are in one tri nket. So if one tri nket equals four blanket s, and three blankets equal seven drink ets, then we can say that four blanket s would be equal to four times seven divided by three drink ets. That gives us twenty- eight divided by three, which is about nine point six seven drinkets per tri nket. But since we're dealing with whole numbers here, it might be easier to work backwards. Let's see, if three blanket s equal seven drinkets, then one blanket equals seven divided by three drinkets, which is roughly two point three three drinkets. Then, if one tri nket equals four blanket s, then one tri nket would equal four times two point three three, which is about nine point three two drinkets. Hmm, but maybe there's a better way. Let's try cross-multiplying. If one tri nket equals four blanket s, and three blanket s equal seven drink ets, then four blanket s would be four times seven divided by three, which is twenty- eight over three, or approximately nine point six seven drink ets. Wait, that doesn't seem right because it should be exact. Maybe I made a mistake. Let me check again. One tri", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 4, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 4, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0115_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "398676f85266d50729c6429f0dc366d23779e24f59f5a0233a09c750dff92983", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.056, 1.1, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.056, 2.102, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.057, 3.101, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.057, 4.104, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.057, 5.103, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.057, 6.103, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.057, 7.104, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.057, 8.103, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.057, 9.103, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.057, 10.103, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.058, 11.105, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.059, 12.105, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.059, 13.105, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 13.1, 13.16, 13.711, 0, 24000, 0], [14, 0, 14.1, 14.158, 14.692, 0, 24000, 0], [15, 0, 15.1, 15.158, 15.693, 0, 24000, 0], [16, 0, 16.1, 16.161, 16.684, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.1, 17.16, 17.714, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.1, 18.162, 18.736, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.1, 19.161, 19.747, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.1, 20.161, 20.72, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.1, 21.16, 21.743, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.1, 22.161, 22.722, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.1, 23.162, 23.651, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.1, 24.162, 24.694, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.1, 25.161, 25.683, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.1, 26.163, 26.702, 0, 24000, 0], [27, 0, 27.1, 27.163, 27.727, 0, 24000, 0], [28, 0, 28.1, 28.163, 28.678, 0, 24000, 0], [29, 0, 29.1, 29.161, 29.648, 0, 24000, 0],