{"id": "q0169", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2235220061, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "A coil of 60 ohms inductive reactance in series with a resistance of 25 ohms is connected to an a-c line of 130 volts. What will be the current through the circuit?\n\nA. 2.5 amp\nB. 0.5 amp\nC. 2.8 amp\nD. 3.0 amp\nE. 1.0 amp\nF. 2.0 amp\nG. 1.5 amp\nH. 4.0 amp\nI. 3.5 amp\nJ. 1.2 amp\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0169.wav", "input_sha256": "40118582d40c337b583cd1369cba354274cbf41755cad11b30fe352f499dfd0c", "input_samples": 400800, "input_s": 25.05, "n_real_chunks": 26, "score": 0.5279, "act": 0.9972, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so this is a question about AC circuits. We have an induct ive reactance of 60 ohms in series with a resistance of 25 ohm s, and we're connected to a 13 0-volt AC line. So first thing I want to do is calculate the total impedance of the circuit. Since it's a series circuit, the total impedance Z will be the square root of the sum of the square of the resistance plus the square of the reactance. That's because these are at right angles to each other in the phasor diagram. So let me plug in the numbers: 2 5 ohms for R and 60 oh ms for X L. So squaring those gives me 6 2 5 plus 3 6 00, which adds up to 4 2 2 5. Taking the square root of that give s me approximately 6 5 ohms for the total impedance. Now to find the current I, I use Ohm' s Law for AC circuits, which is V equals I times Z. Rearranging", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_sa