{"id": "q0215", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3247154408, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "What is \\lim_{x \to 9} ((x - 9)/(\\sqrt{x} - 3))?\n\nA. 9\nB. 0\nC. 6\nD. Undefined\nE. 2\nF. 18\nG. 1\nH. -3\nI. 4.5\nJ. 3\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0215.wav", "input_sha256": "30b10e1411c58f7336067cafc00232e66f65ce4d2299509ea0a93a9203a7b25e", "input_samples": 189800, "input_s": 11.863, "n_real_chunks": 12, "score": 0.8534, "act": 0.996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The result is undefined. Division by zero, like 9 divided by zero, is not allowed in mathematics, so the expression does not have a valid answer. Therefore, the correct choice is D: undefined.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 12, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 14, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0215_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "ba4139d09b7a33da64c5e12cf36872d88f268f9fa82fa63f2f849aa794c5434c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 13.68}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.099, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.057, 2.101, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.057, 3.102, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.056, 4.102, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.057, 5.103, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.058, 6.105, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.057, 7.103, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.058, 8.104, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.057, 9.103, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.058, 10.104, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.058, 11.104, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 11.863, 11.92, 11.966, 1, 0, 0], [12, 0, 12.863, 12.921, 13.353, 0, 24000, 0], [13, 0, 13.863, 13.922, 14.387, 0, 24000, 0], [14, 0, 14.863, 14.921, 15.459, 0, 24000, 0], [15, 0, 15.863, 15.921, 16.407, 0, 24000, 0], [16, 0, 16.863, 16.922, 17.457, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.863, 17.923, 18.457, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.863, 18.923, 19.438, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.863, 19.924, 20.44, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.863, 20.924, 21.462, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.863, 21.924, 22.463, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.863, 22.924, 23.387, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.863, 23.924, 24.479, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.863, 24.922, 25.405, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.863, 25.924, 26.245, 0, 16320, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 11.863, "last_real_feed_done": 11.92, "onset": 13.353, "gate_read_done": 13.353, "fire": null, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "stall_note": null, "stall_first_pcm": null, "local_first_pcm": 13.353, "wait_start": null, "expert_req": null, "expert_resp": null, "relay_synth_start": null, "relay_first_pcm": null, "relay_synth_end": null, "first_any_pcm": 13.353, "first_answer_pcm": 13.353, "session_end": 26.245}, "ttfa_answer_s": 1.491, "ttfa_any_s": 1.491}
{"id": "q0234", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2226845436, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Fernandez is planning to attend an auction of the assets of Cross & Black, one of his major competitors who is liquidating. In the conduct of the auction, which of the following rules applies?\n\nA. A bidder can retract his bid even after the fall of the hammer.\nB. If the auction is with reserve, the auctioneer cannot withdraw the article at any time.\nC. The retraction of a bid by a bidder automatically ends the auction.\nD. A bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer.\nE. The auctioneer can increase the bidding price at any time during the auction.\nF. If the auction is without reserve, the auctioneer can withdraw the article at any time prior to the fall of the hammer.\nG. All bids are final and cannot be retracted under any circumstances.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0234.wav", "input_sha256": "e662b2a591353a619903555c94c49e65ea45bd92dd186a9a270cf319b533006b", "input_samples": 822400, "input_s": 51.4, "n_real_chunks": 52, "score": 0.6386, "act": 0.9996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's go through each option. First, a bidder can retract his bid even after the fall of the hammer. That is not true. Once the hammer falls, it means the auction has closed, so you cannot retra ct your bid at that point. Next, B says if the auction is with reserve, the auctioneer cannot withdraw the article at any time. Actually, in a reserve auction, the seller or auctioneer does have the right to cancel or withdraw the item before the final sale if the reserve price isn't met, so that statement is false too. C says the retraction of a bid automatically ends the auction. That' s also incorrect because withdrawing a bid doesn't stop the auction process. D states a bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer. This is generally true as long as the retraction happens before the hammer falls. E claims the auctioneer can increase the bidding price at any time during the auction. Typically, the auctioneer sets the rules and usually follows them unless specified otherwise, but they don' t typically just raise prices arbitrarily mid-auction. So looking back, the best answer is D: a bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 35, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 31, "feed_lag_max_ms": 543, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 1200, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0234_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "427882f9bd599116f5f41bfb0c718bb0feb72dae47fc9abd209eb62f61dfacf1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 31.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.054, 1.098, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.056, 2.1, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.056, 3.1, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.055, 4.101, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.056, 5.101, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.056, 6.102, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.057, 7.103, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.057, 8.103, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.056, 9.102, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.057, 10.103, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.059, 11.104, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.058, 12.104, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.059, 13.105, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.057, 14.103, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.059, 15.105, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.059, 16.105, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.059, 17.105, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.06, 18